crypto-ffi: do not link uniffi_bindgen into the library

The library depended on uniffi with the "cli" feature only for the
uniffi-bindgen [[bin]] of this crate (uniffi::uniffi_bindgen_main). That
feature pulls the whole uniffi_bindgen crate (Kotlin/Swift/Python code
generators) into the cdylib and staticlib built for the phone: dead code for
the app, and its object file is not byte-for-byte reproducible on arm64
(the only differing code object between two clean builds).

- Drop the "cli" feature from the library's uniffi dependency.
- Drop the [[bin]]: the Kotlin sources are generated by the xtask, which
  uses uniffi_bindgen as a host dependency; the workspace "uniffi-bindgen"
  package keeps the CLI, so Cargo.lock does not change.

Against tag matrix-sdk-crypto-0.19.1 (commit b18166c68bb958a21f0bca8b2d8320cb53583362).
Build-only change, no API change. Not compiled locally (no Rust toolchain on
the workstation).

--- a/bindings/matrix-sdk-crypto-ffi/Cargo.toml
+++ b/bindings/matrix-sdk-crypto-ffi/Cargo.toml
@@ -15,10 +15,6 @@
 [lib]
 crate-type = ["cdylib", "staticlib"]
 
-[[bin]]
-name = "matrix-sdk-crypto-ffi"
-path = "uniffi-bindgen.rs"
-
 [features]
 default = ["bundled-sqlite"]
 bundled-sqlite = ["matrix-sdk-sqlite/bundled"]
@@ -45,7 +41,7 @@
 thiserror.workspace = true
 tracing-subscriber = { workspace = true, features = ["env-filter"] }
 # keep in sync with uniffi dependency in matrix-sdk-ffi, and uniffi_bindgen in ffi CI job
-uniffi = { workspace = true, features = ["cli"] }
+uniffi.workspace = true
 vodozemac.workspace = true
 zeroize = { workspace = true, features = ["zeroize_derive"] }
 
